{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/344404-lunar-form-acquisition-gateways-purpose","id":344404,"title":"Lunar Form-Acquisition Gateways - Purpose?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-18T23:09:24-08:00","id":344404,"title":"Lunar Form-Acquisition Gateways - Purpose?","content":"There's a clear and obvious reason why Humble Mouse Shape and Towering Beast Form exist. Being able to assume very small or very large forms represents a great advantage; so great that it is considered good balance that Lunars must spend XP or an initial Charm choice on gaining that power.<br /> <br /> Likewise, gaining the ability to turn into humans as well as animals is a great advantage.<br /> <br /> But then we get to the various kinds of spirit, and the advantages suddenly dry up.<br /> <br /> Lunars have never been able to achieve effortless immateriality through assuming the form of a god or demon, and probably shouldn't. Elementals are naturally material anyway. Turning into a ghost didn't help a Lunar respire like one in the Underworld, either, nor did turning into a raksha help resist Wyld Mutation. Becoming a Dragon King would never let you reincarnate like one.<br /> <br /> Lunars being able to use the CHARMS of those various creatures is an idea to be thrown right out the window. Now even the Eclipse Caste Solars can only learn specific, Eclipse-keyworded Charms which will all be balanced with that fact in mind... at most, Lunars might be able to enjoy <i>those</i> Charms.<br /> <br /> I'd rather not see the Lunar Charmset be nerfed to account for all the possible powers of gods and other spirits.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, anyway. If a Lunar turning into Ahlat is still naturally material, can't hear prayers like a god, and doesn't have Ahlat's Charms, then is there any point to buying a Knack to turn into gods? Couldn't a Lunar just use a shapeshifting disguise Charm and get as much out of it?<br /> <br /> Or rather, does it make more sense that Prey's Skin Disguise alone would be all you need to take the forms of other sapient beings? You can't take Ahlat's godly features or powers, you could already fake his appearance, so the only things worth taking through his Blood are his Attributes, Abilities and memories.<br /> <br /> A god's dot-rated traits are not THAT sufficiently different from those of an animal or human. Sure, they're generally going to be higher, but so what? You already passed the entry bar by being a badass enough dude to take Ahlat's traits for your own, so your traits are likely already great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T00:37:09-08:00","id":344463,"title":"","content":"Animals are going to have more options these days (like the tyrant lizard having a bite that even the devs described as &quot;pants-shittingly terrifying&quot;), so why assume that the only thing you can do after stealing the shape of a god is look like that god?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T00:39:19-08:00","id":344465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A god's dot-rated traits are not THAT sufficiently different from those of an animal or human. Sure, they're generally going to be higher, but so what? You already passed the entry bar by being a badass enough dude to take Ahlat's traits for your own, so your traits are likely already great. </div> </div> </div>Ahlat has Strength 12, Dex 7 and Stamina 10. That's pretty hefty.<br /> I do think however, that the prereqs for some spirits, especially Gods and Ghosts, are way too high, considering how little you get out of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T01:19:59-08:00","id":344472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/344404-lunar-form-acquisition-gateways-purpose?p=344463#post344463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Animals are going to have more options these days (like the tyrant lizard having a bite that even the devs described as &quot;pants-shittingly terrifying&quot;), so why assume that the only thing you can do after stealing the shape of a god is look like that god?</div> </div> </div> </div>I did consider that, and it would be pretty sweet.<br /> <br /> But would the innate tricks of a god's form be that much different from those of animals? The tyrant lizard has some simple things like the death bite and the ability to track things across an entire Direction by smell alone... a god's form could allow similar or equal abilities, but would any abilities be greater than that?<br /> <br /> And would the abilities of a god's form be significantly different from those offered by a demon's form, or an elemental's? Should we need to buy essentially the same thing three or more times?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T01:41:17-08:00","id":344479,"title":"","content":"Inu.<br /> <br /> I feel that a Lunar who assumes the shape of a supernatural entity like a god, should gain thematic facsimile of that beings character-defining powers as well as innate abilities. Not identical, not as powerful, but something that lets you actually make good use of the form and have a legitimate chance of fooling others. Your own charms should then come to bear and allow you to ply these faux abilities to greater effect.<br /> <br /> Something like... turning into a god with significant cult would allow you to hear the vague cacophony of their prayers, giving you some idea to the potency of the beings cult, but you can't really make anything out. If you significantly enhance your hearing you might get more useful information though. A water gods power might let you pick up and hold water as if it were a solid or a clay. Great strength and feats of strength might let you push aside or divert a river. While becoming a god might not make you truly immaterial, it could allow you to go somewhat transparent or intangible looking, which you could combine with powers for stealth or movement, to do things you otherwise couldn't.<br /> <br /> Basically what I'm suggesting is you take that beings Legos, their essential nature, the basic toolkit that defines them. You then gain the ability to put your Lunar prowess behind it to make people question whether you really -are- that City God when you can swim through the city's mortar and stone like heavy water.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4029-isvarg","name":"Isvarg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4029_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T03:27:06-08:00","id":344538,"title":"","content":"If we can infer anything from Ahlat vs Octavian battle, some gods will have powers dependent on their panoply and legend. It stands to reason, by assuming their shape, you can use some of that legend or panoply for your own means.<br /> <br /> I anticipate with Lunars getting to use the cool powers of animals, they'll be able to use the cool powers of other shapes they take, like gods, demons, elementals, if they can still take those forms. There are few to no general spirit charms now, unique powers for unique beings, and Lunars can use those powers by taking their shapes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":393,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","user":"Godjaw","date":".  Confused Octavian and Oramus, It was late. 12-19-2014, 10:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T06:49:04-08:00","id":344645,"title":"","content":"Bearing in mind that charm costs aren't fixed anymore, those shape acquisition powers will probably have their costs modified to reflect their usefulness, or even be purchasable upgrades or something.<br /> <br /> You might be getting some (if not all) of a beings Merits when taking their shape - it'd be a good way to distinguish between what advantages can and can't come with a shape, instead of the vagueness we got in 2e.<br /> <br /> Although getting a god's cult through a non-lethal avenue (e.g. sex or life of the hummingbird) would be weird. Do you both benefit from it? Are its benefits halved? Does the god notice?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":".  oh autocorrect, how i hate you. 12-19-2014, 09:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T07:30:00-08:00","id":344693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/344404-lunar-form-acquisition-gateways-purpose?p=344538#post344538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we can infer anything from Ahlat vs Oramus battle, some gods will have powers dependent on their panoply and legend. It stands to reason, by assuming their shape, you can use some of that legend or panoply for your own means.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was Octavian. Ahlat vs. Oramus would be interesting, but it wasn't what we got to see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T07:39:03-08:00","id":344699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/344404-lunar-form-acquisition-gateways-purpose#post344404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a clear and obvious reason why Humble Mouse Shape and Towering Beast Form exist. Being able to assume very small or very large forms represents a great advantage; so great that it is considered good balance that Lunars must spend XP or an initial Charm choice on gaining that power.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always seen these as just an XP tax but I guess the justification is OK because you want someone to have a higher price if their spirit shape is tyrant lizard versus lion. I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T10:00:26-08:00","id":344880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/344404-lunar-form-acquisition-gateways-purpose?p=344538#post344538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we can infer anything from Ahlat vs Oramus battle, some gods will have powers dependent on their panoply and legend. It stands to reason, by assuming their shape, you can use some of that legend or panoply for your own means.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose it's possible that just as every animal is designed with the idea in mind that a Lunar is going to turn into it, it's possible to design<i> every spirit in the game</i> with the same idea.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of a GENERAL Knack which allows you to inherit the artifact-attunements of any creature you kill, so you can instantly use their daiklaive. I figure this would be packaged together with the effect of stealing someone's Fate/Destiny, keeping their star from dimming in the sky and thwarting that avenue of Sidereal investigation.<br /> <br /> <br /> BUT -- is a demon sufficiently different from a god in terms of Lunar advantage that you should need two different Knacks for their forms? Demons are like gods in being naturally immaterial, capable of hearing prayers, having panoplies, and being immortal.<br /> <br /> Would either be sufficiently different from elementals, which are like mortals in being naturally material and incapable of hearing prayers?<br /> <br /> What about raksha or ghosts, which have odd relationships with materiality and cannot and can hear prayers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T12:49:58-08:00","id":345050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/344404-lunar-form-acquisition-gateways-purpose?p=344538#post344538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we can infer anything from Ahlat vs Oramus battle, some gods will have powers dependent on their panoply and legend. It stands to reason, by assuming their shape, you can use some of that legend or panoply for your own means.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ahlat vs Octavian.<br /> <br /> Ahlat vs Oramus......wouldn't be the sort of fight I would consider worth busting out dice for.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/ksr/avatars/3507685/Exalted_Back.small.jpg?1370109312\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <hr />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/446-nervaqus987","name":"Nervaqus987","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T13:23:09-08:00","id":345068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/344404-lunar-form-acquisition-gateways-purpose?p=344645#post344645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bearing in mind that charm costs aren't fixed anymore</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh? I haven't heard anything like