an impossible color]<br /> <br /> Ahlat: AHHHHHHHHHHHHHH!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T13:47:16-08:00","id":345135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/344404-lunar-form-acquisition-gateways-purpose?p=345068#post345068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh? I haven't heard anything like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same - while I am sure that SOME Charms might have variable cost for variable effect (in the way that Excellencies do), I truly doubt EVERY Charm will work that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T14:11:27-08:00","id":345143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/344404-lunar-form-acquisition-gateways-purpose?p=344880#post344880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose it's possible that just as every animal is designed with the idea in mind that a Lunar is going to turn into it, it's possible to design<i> every spirit in the game</i> with the same idea.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of a GENERAL Knack which allows you to inherit the artifact-attunements of any creature you kill, so you can instantly use their daiklaive. I figure this would be packaged together with the effect of stealing someone's Fate/Destiny, keeping their star from dimming in the sky and thwarting that avenue of Sidereal investigation.<br /> <br /> <br /> BUT -- is a demon sufficiently different from a god in terms of Lunar advantage that you should need two different Knacks for their forms? Demons are like gods in being naturally immaterial, capable of hearing prayers, having panoplies, and being immortal.<br /> <br /> Would either be sufficiently different from elementals, which are like mortals in being naturally material and incapable of hearing prayers?<br /> <br /> What about raksha or ghosts, which have odd relationships with materiality and cannot and can hear prayers?</div> </div> </div> </div>In-setting there is a very great deal of difference between them. At least between the actual souls of the yozis and gods. It would make sense from a Watsonian perspective that different magic was required to interact with them in a particular way even if mechanically they are almost identical.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T15:14:56-08:00","id":345169,"title":"","content":"Being able to take the shape of gods and demons gives you a palette well outside what exists in nature, which has benefits if you want something that is hard to justify existing in the animal kingdom. It also assists in impersonation, despite being less useful than impersonating a person (especially fun if you keep material demons around, and can assume their shape). That said, it would work a hell of a lot better if you assumed that some abilities like &quot;is constantly on fire&quot; are natural effects rather than charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T17:23:06-08:00","id":345274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/344404-lunar-form-acquisition-gateways-purpose?p=345068#post345068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh? I haven't heard anything like that.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>What We Know Wiki</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Q: Will some Charms have cheaper XP costs than others? <b>(Black Paper Moon)</b></i><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">A: Yes. </span></span><b>(John M\u00f8rke)</b></div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/ExaltedWiki/mediawiki-1.19.1/index.php?title=Charms\" target=\"_blank\">http://avatarcomic.net/ExaltedWiki/m...p?title=Charms</a><br /> <br /> Edit: also<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Q: A sort of general question about charm trees: Some of the older charmsets seem to have a bloat trouble (big offender would be the Awareness tree, where to get super senses you need to buy 2+ charms for each sense.) Is the idea still to buy upgrades to an existing charm or are the trees more individual where each charm is a unique power on its own? <b>(mistaya)</b><br /> <br /> A: I have introduced small upgrades (similar to submodules) that cost less XP to alleviate some of the slog.<br /> I may post an example in this thread later. <b>(John M\u00f8rke)</b> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 12-19-2014, 08:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T19:32:18-08:00","id":345343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/344404-lunar-form-acquisition-gateways-purpose?p=344693#post344693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was Octavian. Ahlat vs. Oramus would be interesting, but it wasn't what we got to see.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Right, thank you. fixing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T19:38:01-08:00","id":345346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/344404-lunar-form-acquisition-gateways-purpose?p=344880#post344880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose it's possible that just as every animal is designed with the idea in mind that a Lunar is going to turn into it, it's possible to design<i> every spirit in the game</i> with the same idea.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of a GENERAL Knack which allows you to inherit the artifact-attunements of any creature you kill, so you can instantly use their daiklaive. I figure this would be packaged together with the effect of stealing someone's Fate/Destiny, keeping their star from dimming in the sky and thwarting that avenue of Sidereal investigation.<br /> <br /> <br /> BUT -- is a demon sufficiently different from a god in terms of Lunar advantage that you should need two different Knacks for their forms? Demons are like gods in being naturally immaterial, capable of hearing prayers, having panoplies, and being immortal.<br /> <br /> Would either be sufficiently different from elementals, which are like mortals in being naturally material and incapable of hearing prayers?<br /> <br /> What about raksha or ghosts, which have odd relationships with materiality and cannot and can hear prayers?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well all of them with have their own unique powers. There are bound to be similarities, but they work differently on principle. Say you have the shape of a god that can heal using Presence, and you have the shape of a sesseljae who can heal with Craft. Both heal, but do it differently, and may have other side-effects or bonuses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T14:07:41-08:00","id":350049,"title":"","content":"Maybe it's stupid, but I think that the best way to both give Lunars the power and flexibility they are supposed to possess, and balance things mechanically, is for them to be able to purchase the personal charms/abilities possessed by beings whose Heart's Blood they possess, with appropriate surcharges and/or limitations to avoid the whole &quot;Eclipsoid&quot; issue. Such as, for instance, Exalted charms drawing upon the Exaltation, of which the Lunar only possesses her own. Or certain Panoply charms being invested in a divine portfolio or spiritual dominion, and thus only remains accessible so long as no one else claims it.<br /> <br /> You kill a Tyrant Lizard, you get to transform into a Tyrant Lizard. But if you want the full benefits of being a Tyrant Lizard, you have to invest the time and effort to master that form. Same goes whether you want to become a Storm Serpent or Ahlat or Octavian; there are no shortcuts to power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Aretii: &quot;As one of the players described it, 'After initiation, it was actually a relief seeing who had eyepatches or bandaged hands - you know what <i>they</i> sacrificed, instead of wondering what bits people cut out of their own souls to gain power.'&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/578-lord-sia","name":"Lord Sia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T14:29:22-08:00","id":350062,"title":"","content":"Personally i think weve been given a bit too much and too little leeway with the &quot;animal&quot; descriptor. Mechanically is there any good reason to take a common dog form over a great terror? Or a common horse over a Samatta? Am i the only one here who felt like they were getting a raw deal playing such basic animals?<br /> <br /> Id like to see form acquisition changed so that the actual power of the form in question was the limiter on its acquisiton. In the Lunar wishlist i proposed the idea of &quot;shifter xp&quot; similar to evocation mechanics that allowed lunars to upgrade known forms, but what about assigning new forms an xp cost, building them up like characters with their own stats and merits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T16:27:01-08:00","id":350137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/344404-lunar-form-acquisition-gateways-purpose?p=350062#post350062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally i think weve been given a bit too much and too little leeway with the &quot;animal&quot; descriptor. Mechanically is there any good reason to take a common dog form over a great terror? Or a common horse over a Samatta? Am i the only one here who felt like they were getting a raw deal playing such basic animals?<br /> <br /> Id like to see form acquisition changed so that the actual power of the form in question was the limiter on its acquisiton. In the Lunar wishlist i proposed the idea of &quot;shifter xp&quot; similar to evocation mechanics that allowed lunars to upgrade known forms, but what about assigning new forms an xp cost, building them up like characters with their own stats and merits?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yah. Or something like - knock on wood - TAW, with it's &quot;Mythic Totem&quot; concept. One Lunar may have Tyrant Lizard totem, and that makes his totem form big and scary - like a Lunar Tyrant Lizard, no more, no less. Another has a cat totem, but her totem form is the Velvet-Furred Stalker of Sijan, which savants debate to this day whether it was a behemoth, hecatonkhire, god, ghost, faerie or demon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Aretii: &quot;As one of the players described it, 'After initiation, it was actually a relief seeing who had eyepatches or bandaged hands - you know what <i>they</i> sacrificed, instead of wondering what bits people cut out of their own souls to gain power.'&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/578-lord-sia","name":"Lord Sia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T16:39:01-08:00","id":350139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Sia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/344404-lunar-form-acquisition-gateways-purpose?p=350137#post350137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yah. Or something like - knock on wood - TAW..,</div> </div> </div> </div>The more you mention it, the less likely it is to show up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T18:01:07-08:00","id":350205,"title":"","content":"Heart-Theft of the Behemoth doesn't actually make sense.<br /> <br /> &quot;Behemoth&quot; is not a species. Mount Mostah and Proto Puma Prime and Arad the Hunter are not related.<br /> <br /> &quot;Behemoth&quot; is a catch-all term for the miscellaneous pile; those creatures who are entirely unique, being neither a member of a demon species, nor an elemental species, nor a god, or a raksha, or a goblin...<br /> <br /> If Lunars can learn one Knack to become essentially anything regardless of classification, then that one Knack would be able to substitute for any other form-acquisition Knack. Because if both Mostah and Prime become valid targets with one Knack, then that one Knack should surely be able to handle blood apes and Dragon Kings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T19:28:24-08:00","id":350299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Sia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/344404-lunar-form-acquisition-gateways-purpose?p=350049#post350049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it's stupid, but I think that the best way to both give Lunars the power and flexibility they are supposed to possess, and balance things mechanically, is for them to be able to purchase the personal charms/abilities possessed by beings whose Heart's Blood they possess, with appropriate surcharges and/or limitations to avoid the whole &quot;Eclipsoid&quot; issue. Such as, for instance, Exalted charms drawing upon the Exaltation, of which the Lunar only possesses her own. Or certain Panoply charms being invested in a divine portfolio or spiritual dominion, and thus only remains accessible so long as no one else claims it.<br /> <br /> You kill a Tyrant Lizard, you get to transform into a Tyrant Lizard. But if you want the full benefits of being a Tyrant Lizard, you have to invest the time and effort to master that form. Same goes whether you want to become a Storm Serpent or Ahlat or Octavian; there are no shortcuts to power.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can see this being an investment of the kind equivalent to &quot;Solar XP&quot; that will be in their book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T19:29:56-08:00","id":350301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/344404-lunar-form-acquisition-gateways-purpose?p=350062#post350062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally i think weve been given a bit too much and too little leeway with the &quot;animal&quot; descriptor. Mechanically is there any good reason to take a common dog form over a great terror? Or a common horse over a Samatta? Am i the only one here who felt like they were getting a raw deal playing such basic animals?<br /> <br /> Id like to see form acquisition changed so that the actual power of the form in question was the limiter on its acquisiton. In the Lunar wishlist i proposed the idea of &quot;shifter xp&quot; similar to evocation mechanics that allowed lunars to upgrade known forms, but what about assigning new forms an xp cost, building them up like characters with their own stats and merits?</div> </div> </div> </div>The common dog or horse is unassuming. That is a strength if you think about it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T19:56:10-08:00","id":350337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/344404-lunar-form-acquisition-gateways-purpose?p=350301#post350301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The common dog or horse is unassuming. That is a strength if you think about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not feel that &quot;how others perceive members of this category&quot; is a valid way to divide the categories which a Lunar has learned to access.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T19:58:53-08:00","id":350339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/344404-lunar-form-acquisition-gateways-purpose?p=350337#post350337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not feel that &quot;how others perceive members of this category&quot; is a valid way to divide the categories which a Lunar has learned to access.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, it seems to be one of the primary reasons for taking small, common animals and gods. The social perception makes them effectively invisible or grants a lot of respectability that the silver anathema lack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T20:24:42-08:00","id":350348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/344404-lunar-form-acquisition-gateways-purpose?p=350339#post350339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know, it seems to be one of the primary reasons for taking small, common animals and gods. The social perception makes them effectively invisible or grants a lot of respectability that the silver anathema lack.</div> </div> </div> </div>But form categorization is about TAXONOMY, not purpose.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, mortal humans and combat-specced Exalts would require different Knacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T21:10:07-08:00","id":350372,"title":"","content":"I agree that being able to blend in is an asset, especially in games where your ST is very serious about the wyld hunt. However what is common and unassuming in one local may not be so in another. A camel totem blends into the Southern territories just fine, but in the frigid north draws undo attention. Its the sort of situational bonus that really is hard to stat fairly as a merit or attribute. Honestly i also feel this way about the appearance stat, though. Point is, while it is a benefit it is nowhere near as valuable as six extra dots of physical attributes that you could get taking an equally valid but scary totem like the great terror. Also there are many cool esoteric beasts that are not really &quot;better&quot; totems like the malfeasean riding spider which have a &quot;kitsch tax&quot; to purchase while providing no real mechanical benefit.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T22:35:17-08:00","id":350462,"title":"","content":"Perhaps &quot;Animals&quot;, &quot;Mortals&quot;, &quot;Supernatural Creature&quot; and <i>maybe </i>&quot;Incorporeal Supernatural Creature&quot; would be enough? With &quot;Really Small&quot; and &quot;Really Big&quot; modifying all of those?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T22:43:18-08:00","id":350465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/344404-lunar-form-acquisition-gateways-purpose?p=350462#post350462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps &quot;Animals&quot;, &quot;Mortals&quot;, &quot;Supernatural Creature&quot; and <i>maybe </i>&quot;Incorporeal Supernatural Creature&quot; would be enough? With &quot;Really Small&quot; and &quot;Really Big&quot; modifying all of those?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what seems sensible to ME.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T19:08:48-08:00","id":351175,"title":"","content":"Again, I'd really rather we placed bars as suitable based on utility and power rather than any of these other descriptors based on &quot;type.&quot; Like if at starting Lunars could transform into &quot;generic&quot; versions of any non-magical species with physical stats not greater than their own plus one, and size equivalent to 1/2 or 1.5x their own, that would be fine with me. Then you would buy a separate knack for creatures of greater/lesser size, one for increased attribute flexibility, one for creatures with magical abilities and one for copying a specific creature rather than a generic version. Thus a burly starting Lunar might take a Blood Ape form at starting, but a tyrant lizard would require a little charm investment. The actual power of the form would be the balancing factor rather than kitsch factor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T14:55:05-08:00","id":353159,"title":"","content":"The distinction between &quot;animal&quot; and &quot;supernatural creature&quot; is a little dicey in Exalted without specific categories to narrow it down. A lot of Creation's normal animals are &quot;supernatural&quot; by our standards, and there's a wealth of created beings whose status is ambiguous. For instance, are Ink Monkeys &quot;supernatural&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T21:27:08-08:00","id":353442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And blood apes, being demons, are magic by default.</div> </div> </div> </div>But in terms of the capabilities of the shape itself, not really more effective than a gorilla or orangutan. For the Lunar's purposes, quite possibly less so, since the great ape shapes are likely to have special effects, as we saw with the tyrant lizard, and blood apes probably will not, since their power is tied up in spirit Charms which the Lunar cannot use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T22:15:29-08:00","id":353469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/344404-lunar-form-acquisition-gateways-purpose?p=353442#post353442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But in terms of the capabilities of the shape itself, not really more effective than a gorilla or orangutan. For the Lunar's purposes, quite possibly less so, since the great ape shapes are likely to have special effects, as we saw with the tyrant lizard, and blood apes probably will not, since their power is tied up in spirit Charms which the Lunar cannot use.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno if that last bit would be so extreme. There isn't a universal set of spirit Charms anymore, so there's no reason every single spirit's powers need to be represented by Charms. As far as Lunars are concerned, I kinda see this as one of the advantages of it: spirits might have some capabilities for Lunars to add to their toys. I mean, we're talking about blood apes, the go-to 1st circle demon for primal physical violence. I'd honestly find it odd if none of their capabilities simply resulted from the nature and use of their physically imposing bodies. As with ordinary animals, a Lunar should be able to use those. I mean, in the 2e core, because of how spirits were modeled, a blood ape had to spend motes on Landscape Travel to increase its movement rate when swinging from trees and vines. I see absolutely no reason why that shouldn't just be represented by its physical form being such that it's faster about swinging from trees and vines, as I imagine will be the case with most primates in their write-ups. It makes sense that a Lunar could still use that.<br /> <br /> Not to say a Lunar would automatically prefer it to any other large, non-demon primate; if some of an Erymanthoi's intended power <i>is</i> bundled up in Charms or the like that a Lunar can't access, a gorilla might generally come out ahead. It still makes sense that a Lunar posing as a blood ape would benefit from that shape beyond appearance and Attributes. I presume the devs have thought about this and will have some rules for which capabilities Lunars can get and which they can't. One way or another, given the emphasis on Lunars' beast-god angle, I expect a given Lunar will not be particularly incentivized to ignore regular animal shapes for those of more exotic realms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T00:14:20-08:00","id":353543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/344404-lunar-form-acquisition-gateways-purpose?p=353442#post353442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But in terms of the capabilities of the shape itself, not really more effective than a gorilla or orangutan. For the Lunar's purposes, quite possibly less so, since the great ape shapes are likely to have special effects, as we saw with the tyrant lizard, and blood apes probably will not, since their power is tied up in spirit Charms which the Lunar cannot use.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I can't weigh in on the discussion about how much of a Blood Ape's power is &quot;weighted&quot; towards charm usage I will say that S.O.S. is accurately representing my idea here. If blood apes have charms or &quot;demon powers&quot; of another type not specific to their physical bodies than I would prefer that the demonic abilities themselves be locked behind a knack or charm purchase, <i>not</i> the form itself just because it carries this description of &quot;demon&quot; which by itself provides no power.<br /> <br /> SO as has already been discussed I think a Blood Ape totem would and should be rare in Ex3 just as it was in Ex2, but for practical purposes such that for the same points you could get a &quot;normal&quot; beast form with much better attributes. Also, specifically as far as totems are concerned, I think totems should still continue to make a statement about your Lunar's character. So if a player wants to take a demon form as their first totem I would want to know what aspect of their life and/or exaltation made this form an important symbol for them as opposed to a basic gorilla which is a bit easier to see being used as an image of power in the human mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T00:25:00-08:00","id":353545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/344404-lunar-form-acquisition-gateways-purpose?p=353543#post353543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I can't weigh in on the discussion about how much of a Blood Ape's power is &quot;weighted&quot; towards charm usage I will say that S.O.S. is accurately representing my idea here. If blood apes have charms or &quot;demon powers&quot; of another type not specific to their physical bodies than I would prefer that the demonic abilities themselves be locked behind a knack or charm purchase, <i>not</i> the form itself just because it carries this description of &quot;demon&quot; which by itself provides no power.<br /> <br /> SO as has already been discussed I think a Blood Ape totem would and should be rare in Ex3 just as it was in Ex2, but for practical purposes such that for the same points you could get a &quot;normal&quot; beast form with much better attributes. Also, specifically as far as totems are concerned, I think totems should still continue to make a statement about your Lunar's character. So if a player wants to take a demon form as their first totem I would want to know what aspect of their life and/or exaltation made this form an important symbol for them as opposed to a basic gorilla which is a bit easier to see being used as an image of power in the human mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blood apes were flat out unavailable for totem shape in 2e, and I'm guessing that they will be in EX3 as well. The only two Knacks that explicitly expanded the range of totems in 2e were Humble Mouse Shape and Towering Beast Form. One imagines that those two specifically calling out their capability while no other Knacks possessed the same callout meant something. With EX3, we have confirmation that there's a Gaian connection, so again, there will probably be no decidedly un-Gaian blood apes as spirit shapes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T09:39:30-08:00","id":353795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/344404-lunar-form-acquisition-gateways-purpose#post344404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, anyway. If a Lunar turning into Ahlat is still naturally material, can't hear prayers like a god, and doesn't have Ahlat's Charms, then is there any point to buying a Knack to turn into gods? Couldn't a Lunar just use a shapeshifting disguise Charm and get as much out of it?<br /> <br /> Or rather, does it make more sense that Prey's Skin Disguise alone would be all you need to take the forms of other sapient beings? You can't take Ahlat's godly features or powers, you could already fake his appearance, so the only things worth taking through his Blood are his Attributes, Abilities and memories.<br /> <br /> A god's dot-rated traits are not THAT sufficiently different from those of an animal or human. Sure, they're generally going to be higher, but so what? You already passed the entry bar by being a badass enough dude to take Ahlat's traits for your own, so your traits are likely already great.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe there should be a charm/knack that allow Lunar to breed Beastman as half-caste of whatever supernaturals in their heart's blood library. So if you invested in those charm/knacks, and successfully &quot;hunt&quot; Ahlats, you can breed Ahlat's god-blooded beastman that will bred true? I am not sure if &quot;Fish or Fowl gestation&quot; line of charms can do that already, but certainly that can be extended. <br /> <br /> There were several mentions of attempts in First Age to replace Dragon-Blooded with either automation and created races. And those fall out of favors because Dragon-Bloods focused on them for terminations.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1561-kanchou","name":"Kanchou","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T09:55:48-08:00","id":353810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kanchou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/344404-lunar-form-acquisition-gateways-purpose?p=353795#post353795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe there should be a charm/knack that allow Lunar to breed Beastman as half-caste of whatever supernaturals in their heart's blood library. So if you invested in those charm/knacks, and successfully &quot;hunt&quot; Ahlats, you can breed Ahlat's god-blooded beastman that will bred true? I am not sure if &quot;Fish or Fowl gestation&quot; line of charms can do that already, but certainly that can be extended.</div> </div> </div> </div>There absolutely shouldn't be and it would do Lunars a world of good if the powers most often referenced as their best/most important/most evocative weren't &quot;what kind of cheesy template bullshit can I mass-produce via fucking.&quot;<br /> <br /> It only harms Lunar themes when Ma-Ha-Suchi's breeding pens are the norm/expectation for every Lunar's advancement, and it only harms Ma-Ha-Suchi's role and presence in the setting when mechanics encourage his methods to be the norm instead of his own psychotic idiosyncrasy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kanchou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/344404-lunar-form-acquisition-gateways-purpose?p=353795#post353795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There were several mentions of attempts in First Age to replace Dragon-Blooded with either automation and created races. And those fall out of favors because Dragon-Bloods focused on them for terminations.</div> </div> </div> </div>And there is absolutely nothing worthwhile to explore in the concept of Lunars breeding things to replace DBs or (probably) Solars building things to replace DBs. It's toxic and honestly kind of insulting to imply that an Exalt can create something that is more worthwhile <i>than another existing kind of Exalt</i>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T11:16:33-08:00","id":353901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/344404-lunar-form-acquisition-gateways-purpose?p=353810#post353810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It only harms Lunar themes when Ma-Ha-Suchi's breeding pens are the norm/expectation for every Lunar's advancement, and it only harms Ma-Ha-Suchi's role and presence in the setting when mechanics encourage his methods to be the norm instead of his own psychotic idiosyncrasy.</div> </div> </div> </div>As with the Deathlords though I wonder how much of the problem were the exalted setting writers taking one small part of the splat and running wild with it instead of leaving those options there for the <i>player</i> to explore. Really there is nothing in the Lunar charmset that I've ever seen that makes them better genesis technicians than Solars, but for some reason the writers fell all over each other including elder Lunars with sex fixations and breeding camps. Imagine if every other Twilight in the canon were a really slamming cook, and how that would color our perception without ever altering the crafting charmset.<br /> <br /> I think having the ability to selectively breed is very on point for Lunars and Gaia. I agree that this has been overplayed though and I hope we see this fixed in the setting of Ex3 with better Lunar characters, not with a charm overhaul of their breeding themes.<br /> <br /> EDIT: but I would like to see more support for crafting <i>besides</i> genesis for Lunars in Ex3 so that Lunar crafters have other options to explore. I think that wouold help even out their genesis fixation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T09:23:34-08:00","id":354811,"title":"","content":"I would also like the return of Lunar better-breeding capabilities (heck, we're stuck with beastmen), but there ought to be limits for sure.<br /> <br /> Maybe (MAYBE) a Lunar could use a Terrestrial's form or Heart's Blood to sire or bear children with the potential for Terrestrial Exaltation, but even if mixing and matching heritages is possible, it would never be okay to breed anything superior to a Terrestrial Exalt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T09:50:45-08:00","id":354825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/344404-lunar-form-acquisition-gateways-purpose?p=354811#post354811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would also like the return of Lunar better-breeding capabilities (heck, we're stuck with beastmen), but there ought to be limits for sure.<br /> <br /> Maybe (MAYBE) a Lunar could use a Terrestrial's form or Heart's Blood to sire or bear children with the potential for Terrestrial Exaltation, but even if mixing and matching heritages is possible, it would never be okay to breed anything superior to a Terrestrial Exalt.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm uncomfortable with this simply because a Lunar who steals a DB's form is not an actual DB with a DB Exaltation (or not intended to be equivalent to that, at any rate). <br /> <br /> But that does cause issues with the explicit shapeshifting/Heart's Blood notions of &quot;you are this specific animal/person that you ate.&quot; It's never been clear if that extends down to gametes and chromosomes. I assume it kind of intends to and that's where you run into problems with not only DBs and Exigents that pass on their power like DBs, but with things like eating a god, ghost, or what-have-you and then being able to have god-/ghost-/etc-blooded offspring. <br /> <br /> I mean it makes a degree of sense if a Lunar who steals a DB's shape can sire DBs, because physically they are that DB (sans Exaltation). But I wouldn't like it, simply because that Lunar <i>is not a DB</i>. I'm more comfortable with a Lunar who is herself a Dynast possibly bearing children who Exalt DB, or that the Celestial Exaltation burns out the Dragon's Blood within her (latter is really preferable to me just for ease of preventing cheesy bullshit) but I cannot see it being a Good Thing for some no-drop-of-DB-at-all Lunar to eat a well-bred Dynast then be able to have children in that form with a normal-for-that-Dynast chance of Exalting DB.<br /> <br /> It just feels wrong and infringing on DB narratives to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T11:15:28-08:00","id":354912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/344404-lunar-form-acquisition-gateways-purpose?p=354825#post354825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the explicit shapeshifting/Heart's Blood notions of &quot;you are this specific animal/person that you ate.&quot; It's never been clear if that extends down to gametes and chromosomes.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's definitely never been the case with souls. A Lunar who dies in the form of a god or Jadeborn does not resurrect.<br /> <br /> It might be permissible for a Lunar who dies in a Dragon King form to be reborn as a Dragon King. Actually, in that case, a Jadeborn might be fine, too.<br /> <br /> Even resurrecting from a god's form would be fine... <i>if the Lunar comes back as a god rather than a Lunar.</i><br /> <br /> In each case, the Lunar still clearly suffers from the death permanently, as he loses his Lunar Exaltation and becomes something that can never again become human, much less an Exalt. At the same time, it's still better than becoming a ghost.<br /> <br /> I like this idea. Especially since it does make becoming a god meaningfully different from becoming an elemental, even if the Lunar doesn't become naturally immaterial.<br /> <br /> Also, because altering your soul-structure through shapeshifting DOES sync with the notion that you DO become the specific thing you become.<br /> <br /> (But since Lunars become normal animals, do normal animals then have hun souls which reincarnate?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}